**Given:**

4 tan θ = 3

**Calculation:**

4 tan θ = 3 ⇒ tan θ = 3/4 ----(1)

⇒ (dfrac{4 sin theta-cos theta}{4 sin theta+cos theta})

Dividing the above expression by cosθ;

⇒ dfrac{{frac{{4sin{{theta }}}}{{{{costheta }}}} - frac{{cos{{theta }}}}{{{{costheta }}}}}}{{frac{{4sin{{theta }}}}{{{{costheta }}}} + frac{{cos{{theta }}}}{{{{costheta }}}}}}

⇒ (4 tan θ – 1)/(4 tan θ + 1)

From equation (1),

⇒ (4 × dfrac{3}{4} – 1)/(4 × dfrac{3}{4} + 1)

⇒ (3 – 1)/(3 + 1)

⇒ dfrac{2}{4} = dfrac{1}{2} 

**∴ ((4 sin theta-cos theta)/(4 sin theta+cos theta)) = **dfrac{1}{2}
